---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Nav from "../components/Nav.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";

const lastUpdated = "April 28, 2026";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy — Bible Seek"
  description="What Bible Seek does (and doesn't) do with your data."
  path="/privacy"
>
  <Nav />
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16 md:py-24">
    <p class="text-xs font-semibold tracking-widest uppercase text-accent">
      Privacy
    </p>
    <h1
      class="mt-3 font-serif text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold text-ink leading-tight"
    >
      Privacy Policy
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm text-ink-muted">Last updated {lastUpdated}</p>

    <div
      class="prose prose-neutral mt-10 max-w-none text-ink-soft leading-relaxed [&_h2]:font-serif [&_h2]:text-2xl [&_h2]:text-ink [&_h2]:mt-10 [&_h2]:mb-3 [&_h2]:font-semibold [&_p]:my-4 [&_a]:text-accent [&_a]:underline"
    >
      <p>
        Bible Seek (the "app") is built to respect your reading life. This
        page describes what data the app touches, what it never touches,
        and how to reach us if you have questions.
      </p>

      <h2>What stays on your device</h2>
      <p>
        Everything you create inside the app — highlights, notes,
        bookmarks, reading position, custom reading plans, memory verses,
        and tags — is stored locally on your iPhone using Apple's standard
        on-device storage (UserDefaults / SharedPreferences). None of it
        is uploaded to a server, and we have no account system.
      </p>

      <h2>What we don't collect</h2>
      <p>
        Bible Seek does not collect personal information. There is no
        analytics SDK, no advertising SDK, no crash-reporting service,
        and no first- or third-party tracking. We do not see what you
        read, highlight, or note.
      </p>

      <h2>Network usage</h2>
      <p>
        The Bible text, lexicon, cross-references, and topics ship with
        the app and are read entirely offline. The only outbound network
        call the app can make is when you tap a link in the "Get in
        touch" form to send feedback by email — your mail app handles
        that delivery; we don't intercept it.
      </p>

      <h2>iOS system features</h2>
      <p>
        With your permission, the app uses iOS notifications (for reading
        reminders you opt into), iOS Spotlight indexing (so your saved
        annotations are searchable from the system search), and the iOS
        widget extension (so today's verse appears on your home screen).
        All three are local to your device.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        If we ever materially change how the app handles data, we'll
        update this page and bump the "Last updated" date above. Because
        the app currently collects nothing, that is unlikely.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions or concerns: <a href="mailto:hello@bibleseekapp.com"
          >hello@bibleseekapp.com</a
        >.
      </p>
    </div>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
